{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Cuts off</b> — and the cutter is one meaning, like 'unwitting' and 'misleading,' wears out his legs and drinks violence that the fool inflicts upon him. Another interpretation: <b>cuts off</b> — from the edge of one, and after cutting off the house, remove the edges, and it is the clay upon the stones. And the meaning: <b>cuts off</b> — distances his legs to the edge and does not walk to his need." "And the meaning of 'drinks violence' — out of violence, for when he sends by the hand of a fool, his words change."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The comment appears to parse the rare word מקצה in Prov. 26:6 in multiple ways; the second interpretation is textually difficult and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:49.477009916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}